  "notes": "new optional user file `Assets/tau/common/tau-meters.bin` (data slot 10, a `TPKB` version 2 bin of up to 64 meters, never in a release zip). A core reads it if and only if its `tau-compat.json` `layout` has the `role` user, `slot` 10 entry for it (its `format` says what it reads); no entry means the core ignores the file. `tau-packs.bin` is a v2 bin now, and `persist_layout` is 2.\nnew user file `Saves/<platform>/<core folder>/tau-meter-settings.bin` (data slot 11: exactly 8,192 bytes, `TMSF` version 1, two generations with a CRC; each core keeps its own). The Pocket writes it at Quit and at power-off, so it is the user's state: **never overwrite, edit or delete it, and keep it across updates and reinstalls of the same core folder**. **No seed is needed and none is shipped**: the slot has parameters `0x22` and the firmware sets the slot's size entry, so the Pocket creates the file at the first edit (hardware-confirmed, `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-M27). `tau-compat.json` lists it as role `user`, slot 11, `seed: false`, format `TMSF` v1 with `bytes` 8192, and `requires_omega.meter_settings_version` (1) is stated only for a release that has it. A reader that knows version 1 may read it; a file of a newer version must be left alone. Reader reference and golden vectors: `tools/meter_settings.py`, `docs/research/meter_settings/`.\nthe platform category of Tau's `Platforms/<platform>.json` changes from `Media Players` to `Media` (the owner groups his media apps there). A tool that matches the category by text must accept both.",
